 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Their slander (6-7) is framed («استهزاء وسخرية», «وهذا من أعظم الظلم والجهل»). The angels (7-8) and the door in the sky (14) are never drawn. A book only for «إنا نحن نزلنا الذكر وإنا له لحافظون». Not glossed: 6:7-8 (As-Sa'di's line echoes 5:104), 12 and 13:1-3 (first-person paraphrase), 15:5-8 (their claim). 11 keeps «وما يأتيهم من رسول إلا…» whole. STAGING v4: 6-8: the deniers (uncountable) in a town at dusk speak and shake their heads; the Prophet is not shown and nobody points at him; the angels are not drawn; a seal on 8:5 (after the word for the angels) and an hourglass on 8:8. 9: believers read in a prayer hall (As-Sa'di: kept in the hearts of his nation), a book plate. 10-13: a former nation mocks (speak, shake_head), turns away (13:1); a footsteps plate on 13:6 for the way of the former peoples; no destruction is drawn; no messenger is drawn (unnamed). 14-15: deniers at night look up at the sky (no door is drawn), then speak and shake their heads; stars on 14:6."
 },
